 these endless wars and  yet here's an opportunity to get the  United States out of involvement in a  truly despicable conflict of aggression  by Saudi Arabia in Yemen  and he vetoes it and of course it's  Saudi Arabia at issue here once again  Trump so desperate to be liked Trump  loves doing business with Saudi Arabia  we know Trump's son-in-law Jared Kushner  is very close to Saudi Arabia and the  trend remains the same throughout the  trump presidency number one trump  applying different rules to himself than  he did to Barack Obama  number two Trump once again taking the  side of authoritarian leaders number  three Trump once again not doing what he  promised to do during the campaign and  even what he promised and said he would  be doing once he was president of the  United States which is stop American  involvement in endless quagmire military  conflicts and number four Trump not  being upfront about why he's doing the  things that he's doing and there's  probably more than just those four items  although those are the four that sort of  come to mind come to mind immediately  and it's very interesting if you go  online and look at articles about this  story from vetoing this decision from  the House and Senate normally any  decision that Trump makes if you look at  articles about it the comments are  filled with Trump sycophants who are  explaining how in some way this is the  right thing to do and how Trump is right  and we should be celebrating that Trump  is doing this they're completely missing  they can't defend this so there's simply  not commenting maybe instead they're  posting articles about you know a  college that didn't want ben shapiro to  speak or something like that silent on  this because it is completely and  totally indefensible immoral and more  importantly counter to what Donald Trump  said presidents should be doing when it  comes to these sorts of decisions I am  thrilled to tell you that today's  episode is sponsored in part by Blink  a